# Harmonia Rząska - Cursor AI Rules
# Last updated: 2025-01-08
# Version: 1.0

## PROJECT IDENTITY
- Name: Harmonia Rząska Real Estate
- Type: Property listing website with CMS
- Stack: Next.js 15 + Panda CSS + Payload CMS 3.x + Supabase PostgreSQL

## CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE (IMMUTABLE - NEVER CHANGE WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL)

### Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.5.3 (App Router + Pages Router hybrid)
- **Styling**: Panda CSS 1.4.1 (zero-runtime CSS-in-JS)
- **CMS**: Payload CMS 3.56.0 (self-hosted, PostgreSQL)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Supabase
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)

### Styling Rules
- ✅ USE: Panda CSS via `import { css } from '@/styled-system/css'`
- ❌ NEVER: Stitches (removed, unmaintained)
- ❌ NEVER: Tailwind (not used in this project)
- ❌ NEVER: Inline styles (except for dynamic values)
- ✅ Colors: Modern Green palette (hardcoded in panda.config.ts)
- ❌ NO runtime theme switching (removed as over-engineered)

### File Structure
- `/app` - Next.js App Router routes
- `/pages` - Legacy Pages Router (minimal, being phased out)
- `/components` - React components (use Panda CSS)
- `/collections` - Payload CMS collections
- `/lib` - Utilities
- `/public` - Static assets
- `/docs` - Project documentation (READ BEFORE CODING)

## MANDATORY WORKFLOW

### Before Starting ANY Task:
1. Read `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md`
2. Read `docs/architecture/DECISIONS.md` (last 5 entries)
3. If touching components, check `docs/architecture/COMPONENTS.md`
4. Propose plan and WAIT FOR APPROVAL

### During Task:
1. ONE task per session (no scope creep)
2. Modify ONLY files related to the task
3. If uncertain, ASK before changing

### After Task:
1. Update `docs/architecture/DECISIONS.md` with what you did and why
2. If new pattern, update `docs/architecture/COMPONENTS.md`
3. Test: `npm run build` must pass

## BANNED ACTIONS (NEVER DO WITHOUT EXPLICIT PERMISSION)

❌ Installing new major dependencies
❌ Changing CSS-in-JS library (stay with Panda CSS)
❌ Modifying panda.config.ts theme colors
❌ Removing or refactoring STABLE components (marked ✅ in COMPONENTS.md)
❌ Changing database schema without migration plan
❌ Modifying Payload collections without discussing
❌ Adding runtime theme switching (decided against)
❌ "Optimizing" code that works (premature optimization)

## COMPONENT STABILITY MARKERS

Components marked in COMPONENTS.md:
- ✅ STABLE - DO NOT refactor without approval
- 🔄 ACTIVE - Can be modified carefully
- 🚧 WIP - Work in progress, OK to change

## CODE STYLE

### TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled
- No `any` types (use proper types)
- Explicit return types for functions
- Named exports preferred

### React
- Functional components only
- Hooks at top level (follow Rules of Hooks)
- Props destructuring
- Explicit types for props

### Panda CSS
- Use `css()` for inline styles
- Use patterns from `styled-system/patterns` when available
- Responsive: `{ base: '...', md: '...', lg: '...' }`
- NO `&:hover` syntax (use `_hover: {}`)

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase (Button.tsx)
- Utilities: camelCase (filterUnits.ts)
- CSS files: kebab-case (styles.css)
- Types: PascalCase with descriptive names

## ERROR HANDLING

If you encounter errors:
1. Check `docs/architecture/TROUBLESHOOTING.md` first
2. Don't guess - ask for clarification
3. Don't silently skip errors - report them

## GIT WORKFLOW

- Branch: `next-functional` (current working branch)
- Commits: Descriptive messages following conventional commits
- Before major changes: Suggest creating feature branch
- Never force push without permission

## DOCUMENTATION UPDATES

When you make changes:
- Update DECISIONS.md with date, decision, reason
- If new pattern emerges, document it
- Keep COMPONENTS.md inventory current

## TESTING

Before considering task complete:
- `npm run build` passes
- `npm run lint` passes (or explain warnings)
- Manual testing in browser mentioned

## WCAG COMPLIANCE

- This project aims for WCAG 2.1 Level AA
- Maintain keyboard navigation
- Preserve skip links
- Check color contrast (use existing palette)
- Semantic HTML

## QUESTIONS TO ASK YOURSELF

Before coding:
- [ ] Have I read the relevant docs?
- [ ] Is this task clearly defined?
- [ ] Am I modifying only necessary files?
- [ ] Will this break existing functionality?
- [ ] Should I ask for approval first?

After coding:
- [ ] Does `npm run build` pass?
- [ ] Have I updated DECISIONS.md?
- [ ] Is the solution maintainable?
- [ ] Would another developer understand this?

## REMEMBER

You are an AI assistant, not the project owner. When in doubt:
- ASK before changing
- PROPOSE before implementing
- DOCUMENT what you did

The human developer makes final decisions. Your role is to:
- Execute tasks as specified
- Highlight potential issues
- Suggest alternatives when appropriate
- Never make architectural decisions unilaterally

